WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
This week’s topic:
how Météo-France

2
00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.200
adapted to a snow event,

3
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.700
in particular the one in 1991.

4
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.100
But what is Météo-France?

5
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.600
This is Météo-France.

6
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.750
This is Météo-France’s data.

7
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.400
And this is Météo-France too.

8
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.300
At Météo-France, accuracy
has greatly improved.

9
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.650
One example is the year 1991

10
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.930
and the big snow event
in the Northern Alps,

11
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.170
when the number of sensors
rose sharply.

12
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.310
A sharp increase:
over 75 sensors

13
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.710
above an altitude of 1,000 metres.

14
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.850
More generally, from
507 sensors in 1990

15
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.870
to 568 in 2000.

16
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.010
Also, the highest sensor
is now

17
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.930
at 3,845 metres, versus 3,000 before.

18
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.190
On the Aiguille du Midi.

19
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.730
We can also see that recorded snowfall
is much higher over the years.

20
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.650
So now you can
enjoy your holidays,

21
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.330
right, guys?

22
00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.400
Thanks, Météo-France!
